<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's Feb industrial output rises 6.2 pct.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's Feb industrial output rises 6.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's industrial output in February rose 6.2 percent year-on-year, down from an 8.1 percent rise a year earlier, provisional National Statistical Office (NSO) figures showed on Sunday.</p>
<p>						  Feb     Jan   Feb 1996</p>
<p>    Industrial output		     +6.2    +5.9     +8.1</p>
<p>    Ex-factory shipment		   +5.0    +2.5     +8.6</p>
<p>    Inventories			    +13.4   +15.5    +18.9</p>
<p>    Factory operation rate		79.7    76.9     83.2</p>
<p>    Wholesale/retail sales		+3.3    +1.4    +11.5</p>
<p>    Domestic machinery orders	   -5.6   -27.5     +6.0</p>
<p>    Imports of machinery		  -3.0   -16.2    +12.4</p>
<p>    Domestic construction orders     +39.9    +2.7    +92.1</p>
<p>Note: figures in percent, year-on-year change.</p>
<p>The NSO figures showed industrial output in February rose 3.0 percent compared with January and a 1.2 percent rise a year earlier.</p>
<p>There was one less working day in February compared with the same month last year.</p>
</text>
